@startuml crc
' Source: docs/design/requirements.md, section "CRC Analysis" (generated from its tables)
' CRC cards only: no relationship arrows between cards.
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle

class CurrencyPair {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its name (for example, EUR_USD)
  Know its past price data
  Know its current market structure
  Know its pip size (0.01 for a JPY pair, 0.0001 otherwise)
  Know its pip value per standard lot in USD at a price, and reject a cross pair (FR9)
  Know its backtest results, add or remove one, and know its most recent (the one added last)
  Accept only a backtest result for itself (the same object) that it does not already hold and that is not dated earlier than its most recent
  .. Collaborators ..
  BacktestResult
}

class TradeSetup {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know which currency pair it belongs to
  Know its trade direction, and whether it is a buy or a sell
  Know its entry price, stop loss, and take profit, in the price order its direction requires (FR2)
  Know its reward, its risk, and its reward-to-risk ratio
  Know its outcome (win, loss, or open) on its pair's price data (FR3)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  TradeDirection
}

class TradeDirection {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know whether it is buy or sell (kind comes from BuyDirection or SellDirection)
  Check the price order of an entry, a stop loss, and a take profit
  Know the reward and the risk for an entry, a stop loss, and a take profit
  Know the outcome (win, loss, or open) of a stop loss and a take profit on price data
  Know whether one price is beyond another in the trade's favor
  Know its units sign
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class BuyDirection {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know that it is buy
  Require stop loss < entry < take profit
  Know the reward (take profit − entry) and the risk (entry − stop loss)
  Know the outcome: a win when a high reaches take profit, a loss when a low reaches stop loss
  Know that a price is beyond another when it is higher, and that its units sign is positive
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class SellDirection {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know that it is sell
  Require take profit < entry < stop loss
  Know the reward (entry − take profit) and the risk (stop loss − entry)
  Know the outcome: a win when a low reaches take profit, a loss when a high reaches stop loss
  Know that a price is beyond another when it is lower, and that its units sign is negative
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class BacktestResult {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know which currency pair was tested
  Know which trade setups were tested, and add or remove one
  Accept only a trade setup on its own currency pair (the same object) that it does not already hold
  Know its number of setups tested, trades, and wins from each setup's outcome; open setups are not trades (FR3)
  Know its win rate: wins divided by trades
  Know when the test was run
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  TradeSetup
}

class Candle {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its currency pair and timeframe
  Know its time, open, high, low, close, and volume
  Reject an incomplete candle, a high below its low, an open or close outside [low, high], and any price <= 0 (FR6)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  Timeframe
}

class SwingPoint {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its currency pair and timeframe
  Know its time, its price, and whether it is a high or a low
  Know its label: HH or LH for a high, HL or LL for a low (FR7)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  Timeframe
}

class StructureEvent {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the swing point it broke
  Know the time and the close price of the break
  Know its direction, bullish or bearish (kind comes from BreakOfStructure or ChangeOfCharacter)
  Require the close to be beyond the swing point's price in its direction
  .. Collaborators ..
  SwingPoint
}

class BreakOfStructure {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Require the broken swing point to be an HH (bullish) or an LL (bearish)
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class ChangeOfCharacter {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Require the broken swing point to be an LH (bullish) or an HL (bearish)
  .. Collaborators ..
}

class TimeframeAnalysis {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its currency pair and timeframe
  Know its trend: uptrend, downtrend, or ranging, as computed by the analysis tool from its swing labels (FR12)
  Know its most recent structure event, if any, on its own currency pair and timeframe
  Know its vote (bullish, bearish, or neutral) from its trend and its most recent structure event (see Voting)
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  Timeframe
  StructureEvent
}

class Signal {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its M1, M5, H1, and H4 analyses, all for the same currency pair
  Know its direction: the majority of the bullish and bearish votes, or no direction on a tie
  Know its score: the number of timeframes voting its direction (0 when it has no direction)
  Know its minimum confluence score, a whole number from 1 to 4 (default 3)
  Know whether it is valid: it has a direction and its score is at least the minimum (FR8)
  Know its trade direction: a BuyDirection when bullish, a SellDirection when bearish, none with no direction
  Know its reference timeframe: the highest timeframe that voted with its direction, in the order H4, H1, M5, M1 (FR9)
  .. Collaborators ..
  TimeframeAnalysis
  TradeDirection
  Timeframe
}

class TradePlan {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the valid signal it is based on
  Own a trade setup with its entry, stop loss, and take profit (TP1), in the signal's trade direction
  Know its TP2, beyond TP1 in its trade direction
  Reject a reward-to-risk ratio (to TP1) below 2, rounded to 2 decimals before comparing (FR2)
  Know its lot size and its stop-loss distance in pips
  Know its risk amount: lot size × stop-loss pips × pip value per lot, rounded to cents (FR9)
  Require its risk amount not to exceed the account's maximum risk amount (FR9)
  Require a USD account and reject a cross pair (FR9)
  Require a lot size of at least 0.01, in steps of 0.01 (FR9)
  Know its reference timeframe from its signal (FR9)
  .. Collaborators ..
  Signal
  TradeSetup
  TradeDirection
  CurrencyPair
  Account
}

class TradePlanBuilder {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Collect a trade plan's signal, account, entry, stop loss, TP1, TP2, and lot size, one part at a time
  Build the TradePlan, or reject a build with any part missing, naming the missing parts
  Add no rules of its own: the TradePlan it builds does all the validation
  .. Collaborators ..
  TradePlan
}

class Account {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know its account ID, balance, and currency
  Know its environment and reject any environment other than practice (FR5)
  Know its risk percent, greater than 0 and at most 2 (FR9)
  Know its maximum risk amount per trade
  Know its trades, add or remove one, and know its open and its closed trades (FR11)
  Accept only a trade whose order is for this account and has no recorded trade yet (one trade per order)
  Replace an open trade it holds with the closed trade for the same order (FR11)
  .. Collaborators ..
  Trade
  Order
}

class Order {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the trade plan it was created from
  Know the account it is for, which must be its trade plan's account and a practice account (FR10)
  Know that its type is market
  Require the trader's explicit confirmation (FR10)
  Know its units: lot size × 100,000 times its direction's units sign (positive for a buy, negative for a sell)
  .. Collaborators ..
  TradePlan
  Account
  TradeDirection
}

class Trade {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Know the order that opened it
  Know its outcome: win, loss, or open (FR11), where a win has an R multiple above 0 and a loss an R multiple below 0
  Know its exit price once closed
  Know its R multiple (FR11): the price move from entry to exit in its trade direction, divided by its setup's risk; none while open
  .. Collaborators ..
  Order
  TradeDirection
}

class "rank_pairs (function)" as rank_pairs {
  .. Responsibilities ..
  Rank currency pairs by the win rate of each pair's most recent backtest result; pairs with no result or zero trades last; ties keep input order (FR4)
  Reject a currency pair passed more than once
  .. Collaborators ..
  CurrencyPair
  BacktestResult
}
@enduml
